templates.hand_pose:
{style}

The right hand and forearm of a child of about 7, light brown skin, a little more brown than beige (around #B4754A to #C6885C), smooth and stylised, resting on a plain pale worktop. Camera: orthographic top-down view, camera directly overhead looking straight down at the worktop at 90 degrees; we see only the BACK of the hand (palm facing down, against the worktop), never the palm; the forearm lies flat along the worktop and enters from the bottom edge of the frame, pointing up towards the top edge; no horizon, no sides, the hand is not raised or upright. Pose: {pose}. No tool or object in the hand. Sleeve: a cream cotton kurta cuff with a band of red Kutch embroidery (small mirror-work dots allowed), ending at the bottom frame edge. This is the master reference hand every other hand pose and reskin is made from. Transparent background: hand and forearm only, with only a faint soft contact shadow where it touches the worktop; no other body parts.

{negative}

